The exact licence text recorded for each dataset is in the `provenance.license`
field of frontend/public/data/real/zones/*/analysis/analysis.json and in
pipelines/analysis/README.md:
- NISAR data products (NASA/JPL-ISRO, distributed by ASF DAAC): SME2, GCOV and
  GUNW, used to build the overlays and analysis grids in frontend/public/data/.
- SMAP soil moisture (NASA, NSIDC DAAC), zone-level series.
- Sentinel-2 L2A: contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2026.
- Copernicus DEM GLO-30: produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 (c) DLR e.V.
  2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under
  COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved.
- SoilGrids 2.0 (ISRIC - World Soil Information), CC BY 4.0.
- Weather and climate data by Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0), based on ERA5 and
  ERA5-Land (Copernicus Climate Change Service).
- Crop requirements: (c) FAO, ECOCROP database (https://ecocrop.apps.fao.org/),
  used under FAO terms for study, research and non-commercial purposes, citing
  FAO as the source.
- Agro-climatic crop constraint factors (olive and wheat, rainfed, low input,
  1981-2010): FAO & IIASA (2021), Global Agro-Ecological Zones version 4
  (GAEZ v4), https://gaez.fao.org/, used under FAO terms of use for research
  and non-commercial purposes, citing FAO and IIASA as the source.
- Land cover: CORINE Land Cover 2018 (CLC2018), (c) European Union,
  Copernicus Land Monitoring Service 2018, European Environment Agency (EEA);
  free, full and open access with attribution.
- Suitability class ranges S1/S2/S3/N (85/60/40): LUSET (Yen et al., 2006), as
  reproduced in Selmy et al. (2024), Agronomy 14(11):2601, CC BY 4.0.
- Soil and slope suitability classes (pH, texture, slope, organic carbon):
  Dorronsoro-Díaz, C. et al.,
  "CambioUso", Departamento de Edafología y Química Agrícola, Universidad de
  Granada (https://edafologia.ugr.es/programas_suelos/practgest/olivar/), based
  on Sys, Van Ranst, Debaveye & Beernaert (1993), Land Evaluation Part III:
  Crop requirements, and FAO (1976), A framework for land evaluation. Public
  teaching resource, cited with full attribution.
- Base map tiles loaded at runtime: PNOA orthophoto (IGN/CNIG), OpenStreetMap
  and SIGPAC agricultural parcels (recintos, WMS of the Fondo Español de
  Garantía Agraria, FEGA); their attributions are shown in the map.
- npm dependencies listed in frontend/package.json, each under its own license.
- The optional language model is not distributed with this project; it runs
  wherever the user configures it (e.g. Ollama with gemma3:4b under the Gemma
  Terms of Use).
